From b7fd9fc37bef16165232e4b6dd5aca1ce9362a17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:10:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fleet: revert qwen3-coder complex-type parsing regression
 (upstream #28736/#28742)

Temporary fleet-side revert of upstream/master#28736 ("common: implement
common_schema internal representation for JSON schemas") and its follow-on
#28742 ("chat: improve parsing of complex types in qwen3-coder"), both
merged 2026-09-13 and pulled in by this fork's routine weekly rebase.

The rewritten qwen3-coder tool-call grammar's new mixed-type optional-arg
branch does not reliably bound the closing </parameter>/</function>
sequence: Qwen3.8-27B (this fleet's production model, served via
llamacpp-rpc on gabesrv06/gabesrv10/gabesrv03/gabesrv09) gets stuck
repeating </function>/<tool_call>/<parameter=...> fragments across
consecutive tool calls in an agentic session until the client's tool-call
JSON parsing fails outright. First observed in production opencode chat
sessions ~19-49 minutes after today's LLAMACPP_REF bump landed this rebase
on all 4 fleet models (2026-09-14, log:
~/.local/share/opencode/log/opencode.log). Confirmed unrelated to this
fleet's own GGML_OP_SSM_CONV_SPLIT commit, which touches only
ggml/ggml-vulkan/delta-net-base.cpp.

Revert this patch once upstream fixes the underlying grammar bug --
neither #28736 nor #28742 has an open upstream issue yet as of this
commit; one should be filed.

